-- title:
--   Cocycles with values in a Hopf-module ideal are coboundaries
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $L$ a commutative ring equipped with a Hopf algebra structure over $R$ which is flat as an $R$-module, and let $S$ be a commutative $R$-algebra. Let $\delta : S \to S \otimes_R L$ be an $R$-algebra map which is a comodule structure, i.e. coassociative in the sense that for all $s$ the image of $(\delta \otimes \mathrm{id}_L)(\delta s)$ under the associativity isomorphism $(S \otimes L) \otimes L \cong S \otimes (L \otimes L)$ equals $(\mathrm{id}_S \otimes \Delta)(\delta s)$, and counital in the sense that $(\mathrm{id}_S \otimes \varepsilon)(\delta s) = s \otimes 1$ in $S \otimes_R R$. Let $q : S \to L$ be a surjective $R$-algebra map with $(q \otimes \mathrm{id}_L)\circ\delta = \Delta \circ q$. Let $M \subseteq S$ be an ideal with $\ker(q)\cdot M = 0$ and $\delta(M)$ contained in the ideal of $S \otimes_R L$ generated by the image of $M$. Then for every element $e$ of that ideal satisfying the cocycle identity $(\mathrm{id}_S \otimes \Delta)(e) = (\delta \otimes \mathrm{id}_L)(e) + e \otimes 1$ (both summands transported by the associativity isomorphism) there exists $m \in M$ with $e = \delta m - m \otimes 1$.
--
--   This is the vanishing of the first cohomology of a cofree comodule, in the relative form needed for an $L$-comodule algebra $S$ presented by a surjection $q : S \to L$: every $1$-cocycle with values in a Hopf-submodule ideal $M$ is the coboundary of an element of $M$. It is used in the construction of invariant elements along the filtration of a special formal module by powers of an ideal, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_mem_pow_and_invariant_succ`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_mem_pow_and_invariant_succ), and rests on the structure theorem for Hopf modules together with the cofree case of the cocycle computation.
